  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0 Upgrades the bundled apexsankey core to 1.14.0 and adds opt-in Ignite UI theming: call ApexSankeyIgniteUI.Enable() and diagrams take their node colours, text, tooltip and font from the Ignite UI theme on the page. The add-on is free and needs no license key. SankeyOptions gains Tokens and DesignSystem to turn the shared tokens or the page theme off per diagram, and RefreshTokensAsync() repaints after a stylesheet or theme switch without moving nodes. Behaviour change from the core: an option you pass in SankeyOptions now beats an --apex-sankey-* CSS variable for the same setting; before, the variable won.\n\n      1.2.1 Corrects the package licence metadata. Releases up to and including 1.2.0 declared the SPDX expression MIT, which was wrong: this package embeds the ApexSankey engine, and ApexSankey is a commercial product included in the Pro plan and above with no free tier. The LICENSE file in the repository always stated those terms, so the package contradicted its own licence document. 1.2.1 declares the LICENSE file itself and ships it inside the package. No code changes.\n\n      1.2.0 Ports the apexsankey 1.11.0 option surface into the C# model: type (chord), arcCornerRadius, theme (named or inline SankeyTheme) and nodePalette, orientation, whitespace, axisTitles, viewPortWidth/Height, draggableNodes, particleFlow, nodeTooltipTemplate, tooltipTheme, tooltipFontColor, and a11y. Adds a Plugins option to install the built-in path tracing, time playback, and drill-down plugins. Non-breaking over 1.1.0.",
